KW  - Edge-HyDE
KW  - SLM
KW  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation
KW  - MITRE ATT&CK
KW  - Threat Analysis
KW  - Data Sovereignty
AB  - Automated threat analysis in Security Operations Centers (SOCs) is frequently affected by alert fatigue and the semantic gap between low-level data and high-level threat frameworks like MITRE ATT&CK. While Large Language Models (LLMs) offer potential solutions, their cloud-based deployment introduces critical latency and data privacy risks. This paper presents a proof-of-concept for an Edge-RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) architecture, utilizing quantized Small Language Models (SLMs) for localized inference. To address the limitations of standard RAG pipelines, an Edge-HyDE (Hypothetical Document Embeddings) approach is introduced. Evaluated against 278 real-world Windows EVTX attack logs, the proposed Edge-HyDE pipeline demonstrates a >3.2x relative improvement in classification accuracy over standard Naive RAG baselines. To establish operational viability, a parameter-scaling ablation study was conducted across 0.8B, 2B, 3B, and 14B parameter models. While a 14B localized model achieved 23.2% accuracy, performing similarly with a Google Gemini API upper-bound (24.3%) while strictly preserving data sovereignty, a highly optimized 3B model achieved 15.9% accuracy in just 3.6 seconds. Ultimately, this work demonstrates that while absolute accuracy on raw telemetry remains a challenge, query transformation (HyDE) is an absolute architectural requirement for extracting reasoning from localized edge AI in privacy-sensitive SOC environments.
ER  - 

