AB  - This paper introduces an efficient diagnostic pipeline for the early identification of Alzheimer’s Disease from spontaneous speech utilizing a 1-billion parameter Small Language Model (SLM) Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct. We use a reasoning-based generative framework instead of traditional discriminative approaches. This is done by combining Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) with a calibrated Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting strategy. To tackle the lack of clinical data, we suggest a targeted data augmentation strategy for the ADReSSo 2021 benchmark that keeps important pathological linguistic markers. The proposed method achieves 88.73% accuracy, outperforming BERT-based baselines and larger proprietary models. The proposed system not only has good predictive performance but it also protects data sovereignty by working on consumer-grade hardware and giving clear understandable clinical justifcations. These properties make it a practical and scalable tool for early dementia screening.
