AB  - In the telecommunications sector, automating customer support analysis involves processing vast amounts of sensitive data, creating critical challenges regarding data sovereignty and operational costs. While cloud-based Large Language Model (LLM) solutions offer advanced capabilities, they often introduce prohibitive costs and privacy risks associated with third-party data transmission. This study presents "Lucid," a secure, on-premise LLM architectural framework designed to address these barriers using optimized consumer-grade hardware. The proposed platform demonstrates that software-centric optimizations can unlock enterprise-grade performance without relying on expensive proprietary infrastructure. By shifting inference to a local environment, the architecture ensures absolute compliance with strict data protection regulations (KVKK) while eliminating the recurring costs of token-based cloud services. The findings validate that on-premise deployment is a strategically viable, cost-efficient, and legally compliant alternative for organizations requiring high-volume, secure data processing.
