AB  - This chapter is an inquiry into how artificial intelligence (AI) can transform the present situation of livestock metagenomics into a predictive and prescriptive ecosystem stewardship. It characterizes the biological and statistical anomalies of livestock-related microbiomes at both anatomical and environmental demands, and explores AI methods with representation learning, compositional data analysis, strain and functional rehabilitation, temporal and causal modeling, and hybrid mechanistic-data conditioning. The chapter addresses the addition of multi-omics, sensor, and environmental streams in digital twins to maximize productivity, welfare, and emissions, and real-time edge analytics and generative community design. It evaluates these dimensions of governance as data sovereignty, federated learning, fairness, interpretability, sustainability (green AI), security, provenance, and ethical-by-design protocols. The future involves multimodal foundation models, personalization, space, and single-cell alignment, and the convergence of precision nutrition, welfare metrics, and emission accounting to encourage the production of livestock in a sustainable and minimal way.
