AB  - This paper investigates how artificial intelligence (AI)-driven innovation, the strength of international intellectual property protection, and cross-national variations in data sovereignty laws influence financial system resilience. Leveraging cross-country panel data from 2001 to 2023, the analysis reveals three key findings: First, AI-related technological advancements significantly bolster the stability and adaptive capacity of financial systems, underscoring their role in mitigating systemic risks. Second, the intensity of international intellectual property protection emerges as a critical intermediary mechanism, linking AI innovation to enhanced financial resilience. Third, disparities in data sovereignty legal frameworks exert a moderating effect. These results highlight the interplay between technological progress, institutional frameworks, and regulatory environments in shaping financial stability.
