AB  - Edge artificial intelligence (AI) governance entails creating frameworks that ensure the ethical, secure, and efficient implementation of AI systems at the network’s periphery. This method tackles distinct challenges, including data privacy, security, and adherence to regional regulations. Edge AI improves data sovereignty by processing data locally, complying with jurisdictional mandates, and minimizing latency. The decentralized nature of Edge AI increases the potential for attacks, requiring stringent security measures to safeguard sensitive information across various devices and networks. Effective governance necessitates compliance with ethical standards, transparency, and accountability in AI decision-making processes. Integrating Edge AI with emerging technologies such as the Internet of Things (IoT) and 5G complicates governance, necessitating comprehensive strategies that reconcile innovation with risk management. A comprehensive governance framework is crucial to leverage the advantages of Edge AI while minimizing related risks and ensuring its implementation conforms to legal, ethical, and societal standards.
