AB  - Cloud-based artificial intelligence (Cloud AI) has transformed industries, improved innovation, and provided scalable solutions to complex global challenges. However, these systems’ unprecedented capabilities require robust governance frameworks to address ethical, legal, and societal issues. This chapter examines Cloud AI governance through transparency, accountability, inclusivity, and sustainability. The global and decentralized nature of cloud services raises issues like cross-jurisdictional data sovereignty, algorithmic bias, cybersecurity threats, and data center environmental impact. The chapter emphasizes multistakeholder collaboration between governments, private sector entities, academia, and civil society to create equitable governance models. Cloud AI-specific regulatory frameworks, international standards, and ethical guidelines are discussed. It emphasizes trust through explainability and user-centric design while balancing innovation with misuse protection. The chapter concludes with ways to harmonize governance efforts at the national and international levels, such as the Global Digital Compact. This chapter addresses these dimensions to create resilient and adaptive governance structures that ensure Cloud AI serves humanity fairly and sustainably.
