KW  - Research evaluation
KW  - Evaluative bibliometrics
KW  - Evaluation cultures
KW  - Agreement on Reforming Research Assessment (CoARA)
KW  - Science governance
AB  - The integration of bibliometrics into science governance has fundamentally transformed scientific practices, leading to unintended consequences such as goal displacement and citizen bibliometrics. In response, international reform movements like the Agreement on Reforming Research Assessment (CoARA) advocate for responsible research assessment and the primacy of qualitative peer review. This short communication examines the commonalities and differences of these movements and weighs the pros and cons for research organizations considering signing them. While endorsement offers socio-political legitimacy and can catalyze internal modernization toward improved evaluation processes, organizations are also confronted with certain challenges. These include the potential neglect of disciplinary evaluation cultures, the high administrative burden of qualitative review, and the prevalent risk of purely symbolic uptake. Acknowledging the limitations of current empirical evidence, this commentary concludes that the future of research assessment relies not on universal declarations, but on the development of process-specific evaluation designs. Strategic principles for implementation – such as tailoring assessments to specific occasions, respecting epistemic diversity, safeguarding data sovereignty, empowering evaluation committees, evaluating assessment procedures, and professionalizing evaluative bibliometrics – are proposed to advance responsible evaluative practices.
ER  - 

